  <data name="Tour.Back" xml:space="preserve"><value>Back</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.Welcome.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Your scheduled tasks in one place</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.Welcome.Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>FluentTaskScheduler is a modern front end for the Windows Task Scheduler. Every task you see here is a regular Windows task: it keeps running on schedule when the app is closed.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.Create.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Create your first task</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.Create.Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Choose New Task to run a program, a script or a command automatically: every day, when you sign in, when an event occurs, and more. Folders keep tasks that belong together in one place.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.History.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>See what happened</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.History.Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Select a task to see when it ran, whether it succeeded, and whether it is running right now. The Dashboard sums this up for all your tasks.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.Automation.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Chain tasks and pause them</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.Automation.Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Completion actions start other tasks when a task succeeds or fails. Need a break? Snooze one task or all of them: for a set time, until the next restart, or until you resume them. Both work while the app is running, which it also does in the system tray.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.Library.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Start from a template</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.Library.Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Library has ready-made tasks for common jobs and keeps your own scripts. Quick Actions run everyday maintenance with one click.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.Admin.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Tasks that need administrator rights</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.Admin.Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Windows lets only administrators read or change some tasks. The app lists them, but cannot open them. Start the app as administrator to work with these tasks.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.Settings.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Make it yours</value></data>
  <data name="Tour.Settings.Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>In Settings you choose the theme and the language, what you are notified about, whether the app starts with Windows, and more. The app looks for updates when it starts. You can take this tour again under Settings, About.</value></data>
